# Curated secret denylist for tools/check-secrets.sh — sensitive literals that
# the generic PII heuristics can't infer (your name, third-party/product names,
# anything confidential-but-not-a-pattern).
#
# Copy this to `.secret-strings` (gitignored) and fill it with REAL values:
#   cp .secret-strings.example .secret-strings
#
# One literal per line; `#` comments and blank lines are ignored. Matched
# case-insensitively as whole words, so distinctive names are safe to list.
